-- title:
--   Determinant ℓ of Frobenius on Vₚ J₀(N) for ℓ ≠ p
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and $p$ a prime. Assume [`ModularCurve.HeckeInputsAll N`](def/ModularCurve_HeckeInputsAll.html#L8), i.e. the predicate `HeckeInputsAlong (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) N ℓ` holds for every prime $\ell$, and [`ModularCurve.HeckeOperatorsCommuteBar N`](def/ModularCurve_HeckeModule.html#L25), i.e. the divisorial Hecke endomorphisms `heckeOperatorBar N ℓ` and `heckeOperatorBar N ℓ'` of $J_0(N) =$ `JZero N` commute for all primes $\ell, \ell'$; here `JZero N` is the group $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of degree-zero divisor classes of the base-changed modular function field `modularFunctionFieldBar N` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, equipped with the `HeckeAlg = MvPolynomial Nat.Primes ℤ`-module structure `heckeModuleBar N` (which, under the commutation hypothesis, is the one given by evaluating polynomials at the operators `heckeOperatorBar`). Write $T_p$ for the Tate module of `JZero N`, the group of sequences $(x_n)$ with $p^n x_n = 0$ and $p x_{n+1} = x_n$, $V_p = \mathbb Q_p \otimes_{\mathbb Z_p} T_p$ for `RationalTateModule p (JZero N)`, and $A =$ `rationalHeckeAlgebra p (JZero N)` for the $\mathbb Q_p$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb Q_p}(V_p)$ generated by the image of the rational Hecke representation. Then for every basis $b = (b_0, b_1)$ of $V_p$ as an $A$-module indexed by `Fin 2`, every prime $\ell \neq p$, every valuation subring $A'$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell$ a nonunit of $A'$, and every $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ lying in the decomposition subgroup of $A'$ over $\mathbb Q$ and acting on the residue field of $A'$ by $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$, the coordinates $c_{ji} = (b.\mathrm{repr}\,(\rho(\sigma) b_j))_i \in A$ of the images of the basis vectors under `rationalGaloisRep p (JZero N) (AlgebraicClosure ℚ ≃ₐ[ℚ] AlgebraicClosure ℚ) σ` satisfy $c_{00} c_{11} - c_{10} c_{01} = \ell$ in $A$.
--
--   Since $\sigma$ acts $A$-linearly and $A$ is commutative, the asserted identity says that the determinant over the Hecke algebra of Frobenius at $\ell$ on the rational Tate module of $J_0(N)$ equals $\ell$, i.e. that the determinant of the Galois representation on $V_p J_0(N)$ is the $p$-adic cyclotomic character; unlike the variant requiring $\ell \nmid Np$, the value $\ell$ is obtained at every prime $\ell \neq p$, including those dividing $N$, by using the Weil pairing twisted by the Fricke involution. It feeds the computation of cyclotomic determinants on newform eigenplanes in the Tate module, via [`CuspForm.IsNewform.killedOffLevel_cyclotomicDet_of_eigenPlane_tateModule_jZero`](thm.html#CuspForm.IsNewform.killedOffLevel_cyclotomicDet_of_eigenPlane_tateModule_jZero).
